# Biome formats with `lineEnding: "lf"` and CI runs `biome ci`, which is
# read-only and fails on a mismatch. On Windows `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites
# the working tree to CRLF at checkout, so a fresh clone failed the lint step
# on 45 files that CI reported as clean — a difference in the checkout, not in
# the code.
#
# Normalising here makes the checkout match what Biome and CI expect,
# regardless of the contributor's platform or git configuration.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets git must never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated: keep it out of diffs and out of language statistics.
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated=true
